# Copy this file to ".env" (in the same folder as server.py and client.pyw) and fill it in.
# ".env" is ignored by git, so your secret is never committed.

# REQUIRED. The shared secret that protects all traffic (at least 8 characters).
# The server and EVERY client must use exactly the same value.
# Generate a strong one with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# (Write it on one line, with no quotes needed and no trailing comment after the value.)
SYNAPSE_SECRET=
